{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":550480,"duration_api_ms":545631,"num_turns":54,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dd3bc1e9-5a0b-4481-a012-213df951d90e","total_cost_usd":3.3253385000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":38,"cache_creation_input_tokens":126961,"cache_read_input_tokens":3823588,"output_tokens":23822,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":126961,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":38,"outputTokens":23822,"cacheReadInputTokens":3823588,"cacheCreationInputTokens":126961,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.3010402500000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":2667,"cacheReadInputTokens":25940,"cacheCreationInputTokens":6689,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.02429825,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed the alkalinity depletion validation changes (tanksim-6e5.4.7) across nitrogen_cycle.rs, process.rs, chemistry.rs, engine.rs, tracing.rs, and the nitrification_alkalinity test suite. The core implementation is scientifically correct: stoichiometric constants (NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N = 2/14.007, DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N = 1/14.007) are properly defined and used, alkalinity is charged exactly once per mg N at the TAN-oxidation step (AOB + comammox) with NOB correctly excluded, the carbonate solver translates alkalinity depletion into mechanistic pH decline, budget/tracing surfaces alkalinity deltas with per-system attribution, and the denitrification return path is prepared via alkalinity_produced_meq. All 6 nitrification_alkalinity tests pass. All 21 chemistry tests pass. One pre-existing or recently introduced save/load determinism test fails (save_load_with_active_cycle_state), which is a real regression that must be fixed.","amendments":[{"body":"Fix failing test `save_load_with_active_cycle_state` in `crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs`. The test demonstrates a save/load determinism regression: after saving, loading, and continuing for 48 hours, the resumed engine diverges from the uninterrupted engine (differences in ammonia, nitrite, nitrifier biomass, habitat registry, etc.). The likely root cause is that `Engine::from_parts` (engine.rs:124-125) calls `state.refresh_habitat_registry()` which re-derives habitat values that may not exactly match the serialized state's cached habitat registry, introducing a small floating-point divergence that accumulates over subsequent ticks. The fix should ensure the loaded engine starts from an identical state to the saved engine — either by skipping the refresh in the save/load path or by ensuring the refresh produces bit-identical output.","rationale":"This is a correctness/determinism bug. Save/load roundtrips must produce identical simulation results to uninterrupted runs. The test exists specifically to enforce this invariant and it is currently failing. Divergent simulation state after save/load undermines reproducibility and could produce different gameplay outcomes depending on when the user saves/quits."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"43e693df-de84-4558-b022-cc3216dc441c"}
